  "base_commit": "fab553e97e9052d325336571531261c4cc3faf1c",
  "pr_number": 1401,
  "issue_number": 1400,
  "issue_title": "gap_outlook: CLI dumps a traceback on a directory (or unreadable) artifact path instead of a clean error",
  "issue_body": "### Summary\n\n`scripts/gap_outlook.py::load_artifact` catches only `FileNotFoundError` (plus `json.JSONDecodeError`), so an artifact path that is a **directory** or an **unreadable file** raises an uncaught `OSError` subclass and dumps a raw traceback instead of the module's usual clean `exit 2`.\n\n```\npython -m scripts.gap_outlook some_directory/\n# -> IsADirectoryError (POSIX) / PermissionError (Windows) traceback, exit code 1\n```\n\n`open(<dir>)` raises `IsADirectoryError` on POSIX and `PermissionError` on Windows; an unreadable file raises `PermissionError`. Both are `OSError` subclasses, not `FileNotFoundError`, so they escape the handler.\n\n### Expected\n\nA directory / unreadable / otherwise-unopenable path should exit `2` with an actionable message, matching the already-fixed `scripts/objective_integrity` (#1377) and `scripts/composite_spread` (#1369).\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-11T03:23:46.000Z",
